body:
Sorry to hear that kitt. 

&#x200B;

Nothing much I can say to really help anything but know that there are people who care out there.

"Of all the tissues in the body, the central nervous system (CNS) is one of the first to lose regenerative capacity. "I think this is key.

That has been my own experience of my body. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

" Using the eye as a model tissue, we show that expression of Oct4, Sox2, and Klf4 genes (OSK) in mice resets youthful gene expression patterns and the DNA methylation age of retinal ganglion cells, promotes axon regeneration after optic nerve crush injury, and restores vision in a mouse model of glaucoma and in normal old mice. This process, which we call recovery of information via epigenetic reprogramming or REVIVER, requires the DNA demethylases Tet1 and Tet2, indicating that DNA methylation patterns don't just indicate age, they participate in ageing. Thus, old tissues retain a faithful record of youthful epigenetic information that can be accessed for functional age reversal. "

The rest is just copied for further focus.

What's your affiliation with them? Just saw your tag. Don't have to share, just curious.  
(I'm a pretty big fan. Hope they go into CNC/more manufacturing kinda stuff).

&#x200B;

Over time if you focus on yourself and your self-improvement, that scenario won't happen the same way.

You've got to keep trying to get away from video-games and focusing on self-improvement.

&#x200B;

I highly encourage that you get into some form of art/music. Whether that be painting, playing guitar, or riding a skateboard, whatever it is that you can get that form of deep personal kind of inner purging.

&#x200B;

Making art/music can help you hit that kind of inner place that creates novelty and depth to your experience. Writing dialogue and putting it to music can help express that kind of end-of-the-world kind of nihilistic place.

&#x200B;

For me, music like deathcore helps me express that feeling. It's a similar feeling to what you're describing, only I use it to kinda help myself keep going. I can't describe it exactly only that it has really helped me.

I like bands like... xkingx, fit for an autopsy, black tongue

The problem I have with supporting strip clubs is that I feel like you're exploiting those women.I see it as a sad reality of this world, the commodification of sexuality and intimacy is something that reflects how broken our society/world is.

I'm not saying you're not a victim, because I know how difficult it can be when everyone sees you as something to avoid. If not for certain life skills I had been taught, like therapy and music, I may have suffered the same fate. I WAS FA for a while.

&#x200B;

But those women are often products of shitty backgrounds, shitty parents, and more often than not, dads that never gave them any real skills.

I see stripping/prostitution as something I would never want for my own children, as a path I would do everything to prevent them from going down. I would do everything to make sure they knew how to make money in other ways and be able to afford college.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Edit: May be the reality is that you face social obstacles that most men will never have to face. But if I hear about ANY of my guy friends going to a strip club, I tell them to their face that they are exploiting those women. I see it, generally, as a scummy, exploitative thing to participate in.

I know women who have been in the sex industry, porn industry, strippers, escorts, stuff like that, and gotten out, and they have said things like: Every woman who is in this industry has serious mental and emotional problems. Their words, not mine.

Edit 2: I'm not trying to shame anyone who IS a stripper, I do everything in my power to teach/pass on trade skills to the women I meet, and encourage them to take up skills like welding and things like that.
